  "text": "MSPCA-Angell | Animal Shelter, Adoption & Veterinary Care\nEmergency: 617-522-7282\nUrgent Care\nReport Cruelty\nSearch for:\nSearch\nVeterinary Care\nExpert veterinary care for every stage of your pet’s life.\nEmergency:\n617-522-7282\nPoison Control:\n888-426-4435\nLocations\nVeterinary Care Locator\nBoston\nWaltham\nUrgent Care\nLow Cost Clinics\nInformation\nRequest Appointment\nPay My Bill\nPharmacy\nDoctor Directory\nFinancial Assistance\nClient Information\nBlood Bank at Angell\nCE Seminars\nCE Seminars\nReferral Services\nAngell Referring Veterinarian Portal\nReferral Form\nPathology Lab Services\nPartners In Care Newsletter\nDVM Directory\nClinical Articles\nCE Seminars\nAdopt\nBringing pets and people together.\nAdopt\nView Adoptable Animals\nHow to Adopt\nBoston\nCape Cod\nNevins Farm\nNortheast Animal Shelter\nAdoption Center Wishlists\nPrograms\nAdvocate for animals, volunteer, or get help for your pet with our compassionate community services.\nGet Involved\nAdvocate for Animals\nFoster Care\nHumane Education\nVolunteer\nServices\nTraining & Behavior\nCommunity Outreach\nLaw Enforcement\nLost and Found Pets\nSpay & Neuter Services\nSurrender an Animal\nCareers\nNews\nEvents\nPress Releases\nWays to Give\nTribute & Memorial Giving\nDouble Your Gift\nPlanned Giving\nDonor-Advised Funds and Stocks\nNon-Monetary Donations\nMore Ways to Give\nDonate\nEmergency\n617-522-7282\nCruelty\n617-522-7282\nPoisoning\n888-426-4435\nLeading animal welfare and veterinary care\nin Massachusetts and beyond since 1868\nSupport Our Work\nOur Purpose\nThe mission of the MSPCA-Angell is to protect animals, relieve their suffering, advance their health and welfare, prevent cruelty, and work for a just and compassionate society.\nLearn More\nVeterinary\nCare\nADOPT\nA PET\nPay\nA Bill\nPHARMACY\nServices\nVetERINARIAN\nReferral\nRequest\nAN APPOINTMENT\nTraining\nFOR YOUR PET\nAdvocate\nFOR ANIMAL LAWS\nOn Any Given Day\nThe MSPCA-Angell is saving the lives of sick and injured animals at Angell Animal Medical Center, placing shelter pets in loving adoptive homes, investigating animal cruelty and fighting for stronger animal protection laws and policy.\nSupport Our Work\nContact Us\nPrograms\nVolunteer or Foster\nOpen Your Heart and Home to an Animal in Need\nLearn More\nSummer Camp at Nevins Farm\nThere is still space for August 10th – 11th – all ages (6-12) are welcome to register for the week!\nLearn More\nSurrender an Animal\nNeed to Rehome Your Pet? We’re Here to Help\nLearn More\nTraining\nTraining That Strengthens the Bond With Your Pet\nLearn More\nCommunity Outreach\nSupporting Pets and People Across Our Community\nLearn More\nAdvocate for Animals\nEnsure laws and policies protect animals and the human-animal bond\nLearn More\nLoad More\n2025 Impact\nSupport Our Work\nDONATE NOW\n2025 Impact\n0\nAnimals Adopted\n0\nVaccines Administered\n0\n+ Million\nPet Meals Delivered\nAvailable Pets\nView All\nSunshine\nSalem\n2 Years\nArthur\nCape Cod\n3 Years\nShelly\nCape Cod\n4 Years\nFelix\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nPeru\nBoston\n1 Year\nMarsha\nSalem\n5 Years\nBlair\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nFallon\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nWoodland\nNevins Farm\n6 Years\nPingo\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nButte\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nAyre\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nChannel\nNevins Farm\n1 Year\nPunky\nNevins Farm\n9 Months\nChurro\nNevins Farm\n9 Months\nJoe\nNevins Farm\n9 Months\nJob Openings\nThe MSPCA-Angell believes that the lives of all creatures–human and non-human–are inextricably intertwined. We believe that our shared commitment to our organizational values of Compassion, Collaboration, Integrity, Service, Positivity, and Excellence contribute to a compassionate and just society in which all people and animals are treated with care and respect.\nJoin the MSPCA-Angell team and turn your love for animals into work that matters. We offer strong benefits, paid time off, mental health support, tuition help, retirement matching, pet care discounts, and room to keep learning. If you’re looking for work that feels rewarding, challenging, deeply human, and always animal-focused, you’ll find it here, apply today!\nView All\nFor Veterinarians\nWe strive to offer the best specialized veterinary\ncare while providing the one-on-one compassion and customer service your clients and patients deserve. Angell’s staff is committed to working with you to ensure the best overall health of your patient.\nReferral Portal\nClinical Library\nReferral Forms\nDVM Directory\nExplore The MSPCA-Angell\nWho We Are\nContact Us\nExecutive Team\nHistory\nCareers\nLocation Map\nWhat We Do\nAbout Us\nPublications\nAnnual Reports\nResources\nSpay/Neuter\nBehavior Training\nReport Cruelty\nLost/Found Pet?\nDonor Info\nTribute/Memorial Gifts\nManage Your Gift\nEvent Inquiry\nConnect With Us\nDonate\nNewsletter\nBlog\nVet Portal\nFollow Us\nThe MSPCA-Angell is a 501(c)(3) Nonprofit registered in the US under EIN: 04-2103597. MA Rescue Organization License #170\nThe MSPCA–Angell © 2026 All rights reserved\nWebsite Design by:\nWe Are Immediate\nPrivacy Policy\nPrint this page\nDonate\nEmergency\n617-522-7282\nCruelty\n617-522-7282\nPoisoning\n888-426-4435\nSearch for:\nSearch\nVeterinary Care\nLocations\nVeterinary Care Locator\nBoston\nWaltham\nUrgent Care\nLow Cost Clinics\nInformation\nRequest Appointment\nPay My Bill\nPharmacy\nDoctor Directory\nFinancial Assistance\nClient Information\nBlood Bank at Angell\nCE Seminars\nCE Seminars\nReferral Services\nAngell Referring Veterinarian Portal\nReferral Form\nPathology Lab Services\nPartners In Care Newsletter\nDVM Directory\nClinical Articles\nCE Seminars\nAdopt\nAdopt\nView Adoptable Animals\nHow to Adopt\nBoston\nCape Cod\nNevins Farm\nNortheast Animal Shelter\nAdoption Center Wishlists\nPrograms\nGet Involved\nAdvocate for Animals\nFoster Care\nHumane Education\nVolunteer\nServices\nTraining & Behavior\nCommunity Outreach\nLaw Enforcement\nLost and Found Pets\nSpay & Neuter Services\nSurrender an Animal\nC